# EXPECT: does not provably precede
#
# Round 57: the round-56 order guard sat only on the DEMOTED arm, and a
# clean numeric module global took the gnm arm one line earlier with NO
# order check -- the exact silent-success class the guard was built to
# kill, one arm over (writer called before the module binding existed:
# VM rc 1 "undefined variable", AOT printed 5 then 1, rc 0). The VM's
# outward-write rule is type-blind, so the guard now sits on every
# outward-routing arm.
#
# This is the envelope shape (the VM RUNS it, rc 0, prints 7): the dead
# if-guarded call makes the order statically unprovable while at runtime
# the binding always exists when the writer runs. `v` stays a clean
# numeric global -- no demotion line -- so this fixture exercises the
# gnm arm's guard specifically; its sibling fixture
# outward_write_before_binding.eigs exercises the demoted arm's.

define setnum(k) as:
    v is k
    return 0

if 1 == 2:
    x is setnum of 5

v is 0
x is setnum of 7
print of v
